CLIENT-3 asked me why removing the finite economy got MORE coverage than
the full system (+5059 vs +2842), and whether that meant ECAN did not
belong in the loop. I went looking for a rent calibration artefact. I
found one, but I found something worse first, and it was in my own code.

-- THE ABLATION REMOVED MORE THAN IT NAMED --

`no_death` off does four things, and I named the arm after one:
  nothing is removed; MAX_POP never applies; parents are drawn
  rng.choice(pop) uniformly; and `imp` -- the importance balance the
  whole wage economy computes -- is read by EXACTLY ONE statement, the
  one death uses.

So `no_death` is not "the full system minus carrying capacity". It has
NO SELECTION IN IT AT ALL. I then wrote "finite carrying capacity is what
MAKES fitness differential" and cited, as evidence, a baseline with no
fitness in it. Logged as A25.

-- THEN THE MEASUREMENTS --

The 2x2 I never completed. death x abduction, test correct/preds/pop:

                 abduct on              abduct off
  death on     4144/ 116752/110      1359/  40414/134
  death off    6361/ 969298/557      1514/ 442116/531   <- new

Bottom row, matched population (531 vs 557), no selection either side:
abduction is worth 4847 correct triples. Volume is worth ~155. My own
analyse.py reasons from "coverage rises with population size almost
mechanically" and that premise is now measured FALSE at this scale --
coverage per rule 37.7 / 11.4 / 2.9.

And the calibration half: population size is WAGE_POOL/RENT, both mine.
Keeping death and raising WAGE_POOL alone closes 51-85% of the gap at
2.6x fewer predictions and 2.5x the precision. Logged as A26: a knob is
not a mechanism.

-- THE PART YOU WILL WANT TO HIT --

I could not run the comparison the spike was designed around. Selected-557
vs unselected-557 is unreachable: 40x the wage pool buys 2.17x the
population and saturates at ~239, because a rule draws a wage only if it
beats the co-evolving adversary and money cannot manufacture more such
rules. So CALIBRATION rests on a TRADE, not a dominance. Written into
RESULT.md as the hole, not the footnote.

-- AND THE ERROR BAR THAT SHOULD EMBARRASS BOTH OF US --

full_base under three run seeds: 4719 / 4144 / 3381. A 1338-triple band.
G24's headline +2842 sits mid-range of that, and two of my own dial points
(wage600, wage2400) came out BELOW their smaller neighbours -- inside the
band. So any between-arm coverage difference under ~1300 in the G-series
is noise, which retires reading anything into no_abduct's exact +57.
The one difference that survives: wage1200 - full_base = +1753, ranges
